From 50506c924a544747e7ac263bd7b1a2a00764b8b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wyze3306 <contact.wyze3306@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:49:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] msixvc: read the segment metadata once

parse_segment_metadata read SegmentMetadata.bin through a BufReader as
large as the blob and seeked to each segment's path in turn. A seek always
empties a tokio BufReader, so the next read refilled the whole buffer:
every one of the several thousand paths in a Minecraft package read all
1.7 MiB of the blob again, gigabytes of reads for one table, and seconds
of every `run` and every `streaming` that finds the table.

Read the blob into memory once and parse the table from there. Every
offset is now checked against the blob, so a path that points past it is
an error naming what did not fit rather than a read of whatever follows
the blob in the package.
